1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Nineties Hollywood Icons — Then & Now

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,149
Welcome to Nineties Hollywood Icons, Then and
Now.

3
00:00:15,249 --> 00:00:21,647
Winona Ryder made offbeat characters feel
instantly memorable in Beetlejuice, Heathers,
Edward Scissorhands, and Reality Bites.

4
00:00:21,747 --> 00:00:27,332
Stranger Things later introduced her to a new
generation without losing that distinctive
intensity.

5
00:00:27,432 --> 00:00:32,206
Meg Ryan became one of the era's essential
romantic comedy stars.

6
00:00:32,306 --> 00:00:43,171
When Harry Met Sally and You've Got Mail showed
how a pause, a look, or a perfectly timed line
can make a love story feel personal.

7
00:00:43,271 --> 00:00:52,105
Johnny Depp built an early career around unusual
choices, from Edward Scissorhands to Ed Wood and
Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas.

8
00:00:52,205 --> 00:00:57,791
His portraits reflect an actor drawn to
transformation rather than a single predictable
type.

9
00:00:57,891 --> 00:01:03,170
Take a moment with these images and remember
where you first saw them.

10
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Three more icons. Look closely at the portraits and the roles that made them familiar.

11
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:08,832
The nineties also made room for stars who could
move between music, comedy, drama, and action.

12
00:04:08,932 --> 00:04:19,584
Will Smith went from The Fresh Prince of Bel Air
to Independence Day and Men in Black with an ease
that made every new role feel like an event.

13
00:04:19,684 --> 00:04:29,595
Halle Berry combined charisma with risk taking
performances, from romantic drama to Storm in the
X Men films and her Oscar winning work in
Monster's Ball.

14
00:04:29,695 --> 00:04:38,493
Uma Thurman brought a cool, precise presence to
Pulp Fiction, then returned to action in Kill
Bill with a completely different kind of force.

15
00:04:38,593 --> 00:04:47,862
These six faces helped define a decade, but their
later portraits remind us that a cultural moment
is only one chapter of a long career.

16
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:59,700
Which early and later pairing surprised you most?
